.TH SDL_HINT_MAIN_CALLBACK_RATE 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_MAIN_CALLBACK_RATE \- Request
.BR SDL_AppIterate ()
be called at a specific rate.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_MAIN_CALLBACK_RATE \(dqSDL_MAIN_CALLBACK_RATE\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If this is set to a number, it represents Hz, so \(dq60\(dq means try to iterate 60 times per second\[char46] \(dq0\(dq means to iterate as fast as possible\[char46] Negative values are illegal, but reserved, in case they are useful in a future revision of SDL\[char46]
.PP
There are other strings that have special meaning\[char46] If set to \(dqwaitevent\(dq,
.BR SDL_AppIterate
will not be called until new event(s) have arrived (and been processed by
.BR SDL_AppEvent )\[char46]
This can be useful for apps that are completely idle except in response to input\[char46] As of SDL 3\[char46]6\[char46]0, SDL will allow a single call to
.BR SDL_AppIterate
to proceed without an event immediately after this hint is set to \(dqwaitevent\(dq, so apps can have a minimum of activity, perhaps to render an initial image to a window before the user has otherwise interacted with the app\[char46]
.PP
On some platforms, or if you are using
.BR SDL_main
instead of
.BR SDL_AppIterate ,
this hint is ignored\[char46] When the hint can be used, it is allowed to be changed at any time\[char46]
.PP
This defaults to 0, and specifying NULL for the hint\(aqs value will restore the default\[char46]
.PP
This doesn\(aqt have to be an integer value\[char46] For example, \(dq59\[char46]94\(dq won\(aqt be rounded to an integer rate; the digits after the decimal are actually respected\[char46]
.PP
This hint can be set anytime\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

